---
import chapter from "../../../../data/project/stage3_pass34_money_markets_ownership.json";

const spine = chapter.integration_spine?.chain || [];
const testQs = chapter.extraction_test?.questions || [];
---

<figure class="viz viz--flywheel" data-viz="prosperity-extraction" id="leakage">
  <figcaption class="viz__cap">
    <span class="viz__family">Prosperity vs Extraction Cycle</span>
    <span class="viz__q">Identical-looking activity can produce opposite ownership outcomes</span>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="fly-grid">
    <div class="fly-card fly-card--up">
      <h3>Prosperity cycle</h3>
      <p>{spine.join(" → ")}</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
        While government protects competitive markets and democracy prevents capital from purchasing the rules.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="fly-card fly-card--down">
      <h3>Extraction cycle</h3>
      <p>
        Activity without retained capacity → external surplus capture → weak ownership base → underinvestment →
        dependency → weaker competition → more extraction.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">Extraction Test (MODEL):</p>
      <ul style="margin:0.35rem 0 0;padding-left:1.1rem;font-size:0.88rem;">
        {testQs.slice(0, 4).map((q: string) => <li>{q}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="viz__note">
    Precision, not anti-corporate rhetoric. Large firms can raise productivity; the concern is rents and rule-purchase
    inconsistent with competitive markets.
  </p>
</figure>
